{"type":"cards","design":"S_024","title":"Agent workload and cognitive fatigue","lead":"High disruption volumes and manual policy lookups strain frontline airport staff.","items":[{"title":"Cognitive switching overhead","text":"Agents constantly shift attention between distressed passengers at the podium, departure control alerts, and complex terminal syntax during irregular operations.","icon":"brain"},{"title":"Policy lookup friction","text":"Locating exact waiver codes, baggage transfer rules, and partner carrier agreements under time pressure slows down decision speed and increases error risk.","icon":"book"},{"title":"Queue and attrition pressure","text":"Rising interaction volumes, talent shortages, and frontline employee attrition intensify the daily workload for experienced gate personnel during peak travel windows.","icon":"team"}],"notes":"McKinsey research highlights that airlines and customer support organizations face persistent operational friction driven by rising interaction volumes, talent shortages, and frontline employee attrition. Deploying co-pilot architectures in customer workflows delivers immediate efficiency gains by mitigating cognitive fatigue for frontline staff and accelerating resolution of complex exceptions.

