{"type":"process","design":"S_001","title":"Agentic rebooking workflow steps","lead":"A four-step agentic workflow automates policy evaluation, itinerary generation, and reassignment.","items":[{"title":"Detect connection risk","text":"The assistant ingests live flight telemetry to flag passengers with tight or broken connections before they reach the podium, grouping travellers by cabin and loyalty status. This early prioritization prevents gate congestion and ensures immediate handling for high-tier members.","icon":"alert-circle"},{"title":"Evaluate policy rules","text":"Vertex AI checks fare class entitlements, partner carrier agreements, and irregular operations waivers through Vertex AI Search to determine eligible recovery options. This automated verification reduces manual policy lookups while enforcing compliance with active airline rules.","icon":"scales"},{"title":"Generate ranked itineraries","text":"The agentic engine queries live seat inventory to assemble complete routing alternatives that preserve group travel, special service requests, and baggage transfer windows. It balances multiple flight legs and ground connection times to maintain passenger comfort and journey continuity.","icon":"route"},{"title":"Execute passenger reassignment","text":"Once the gate agent approves an option, the workflow reissues tickets, updates seat maps, and dispatches updated boarding passes to the Fly Delta app. Travelers receive instant push notifications with their revised gate details and itineraries.","icon":"check-circle"}],"notes":"During irregular operations, gate agents face intense time pressure to resolve complex itinerary changes. This four-step agentic workflow automates the multi-step logistics of detecting connection risks, verifying fare and waiver policies via Vertex AI Search, and assembling valid seat matches across available flights. The system prepares the complete transaction so the agent can confirm reassignments and notify passengers immediately.

