{"type":"comparison","design":"N_006","title":"Conversational UI versus agentic action","lead":"Goal-oriented agentic workflows replace passive text lookup with policy-constrained execution.","left":{"label":"Passive conversational UI","title":"Information retrieval only","points":["Requires agents to type multi-turn text queries during busy gate boarding","Returns static policy excerpts that staff must interpret manually","Leaves seat availability lookups and fare calculations to the agent","Forces manual copy-and-paste into legacy reservation terminal screens","Handles one passenger query at a time without proactive disruption alerts"]},"right":{"label":"Goal-oriented agentic workflow","title":"Policy-constrained task execution","points":["Triggers automatically from live flight delay and connection telemetry","Evaluates irregular operations waiver rules and SkyMiles tier priority","Queries live seat inventory to build complete, bookable itineraries","Stages ticket reissuance and baggage rerouting for single-click approval","Processes entire disrupted flight manifests concurrently in the background"]},"notes":"Travel providers are shifting from simple conversational interfaces to goal-oriented agentic models that execute complex, policy-constrained tasks. While a traditional chatbot requires a gate agent to type questions and manually key changes into reservation screens, an agentic workflow on Vertex AI proactively evaluates rules, checks seat inventory, and stages the complete rebooking transaction for rapid approval.

