{"type":"process","design":"S_004","title":"15 percent fewer missed connections","lead":"Predictive arrival tracking and automated protection workflows preserve downline passenger journeys.","items":[{"title":"Inbound delay detection","text":"Streaming flight telemetry identifies incoming aircraft experiencing air traffic or gate hold delays that threaten minimum connection times for transfer passengers.","icon":"airplane"},{"title":"Connection risk scoring","text":"Vertex AI calculates real-time terminal transit durations between arrival and departure gates, flagging passengers at high risk of missing their next leg.","icon":"gauge"},{"title":"Proactive hold or protect","text":"The assistant recommends brief departure holds when operational buffers allow or stages backup seats on the next available flight before the inbound lands.","icon":"shield-user"},{"title":"Synchronized gate alerts","text":"Podium screens notify downline gate agents of approaching transfer passengers and trigger automated mobile updates to guide travelers directly to their new gate.","icon":"phone-wifi"}],"notes":"Reaching 15 percent fewer missed connections depends on acting before an inbound flight touches down. By combining real-time flight telemetry with gate-to-gate walking times, the assistant stages backup seats or coordinates brief departure holds.

