{"type":"table","design":"E_004","title":"Key risks and how we mitigate them","lead":"Proactive engineering controls and operational fallbacks protect gate performance against disruption.","columns":["Risk title","Operational impact","Mitigation strategy"],"rows":[["Reservation system latency","Slow API responses delay rebooking recommendations during peak concourse disruption.","Cache frequent route availability in Memorystore for Redis and pre-compute rebooking options."],["Inaccurate policy guidance","Incorrect fare or waiver rules cause invalid ticket reissues and passenger friction.","Ground Vertex AI Search strictly in approved airline manuals and enforce deterministic validation rules."],["Podium adoption friction","Gate agents revert to legacy terminal commands during high-stress irregular operations.","Co-design tools with hub champions and embed the assistant directly inside existing podium screens."],["Peak storm traffic spikes","Systemic weather events overload inference endpoints across multiple hub airports simultaneously.","Configure auto-scaling on Google Kubernetes Engine and provision dedicated Vertex AI throughput."],["Downstream write failures","Interrupted transactions leave passenger itineraries or seat assignments in an incomplete state.","Require explicit agent confirmation and use idempotent transaction queues that retry or roll back cleanly."]],"notes":"Deploying agentic workflows into live airport operations requires strict technical and operational safeguards. Each risk is paired with an engineering fix, from caching inventory in Memorystore for Redis to enforcing deterministic policy checks.

