{"type":"statement","design":"ENGINE_STATEMENT_POINTS","title":"Frontline efficiency and fatigue mitigation","lead":"Co-pilot architectures reduce cognitive strain on gate staff while accelerating complex exception handling.","statement":"Co-pilot workflows mitigate cognitive fatigue for frontline staff and accelerate resolution of complex operational exceptions.","text":"Airlines face persistent operational friction from rising interaction volumes, talent shortages, and frontline attrition during flight disruptions.","points":[{"title":"Lower cognitive load","text":"Synthesizing passenger context and policy rules on one screen removes mental strain during back-to-back flight delays, allowing staff to resolve issues faster."},{"title":"Faster exception handling","text":"Pre-validated rebooking paths allow staff to resolve multi-leg disruptions and special service requests without supervisor escalation."},{"title":"Sustained team retention","text":"Equipping gate personnel with responsive digital tools reduces workplace burnout and supports long-term frontline stability across high-volume departure hubs."}],"notes":"Research from McKinsey shows that airlines face persistent operational friction from rising interaction volumes, talent shortages, and frontline employee attrition. Deploying co-pilot architectures directly mitigates cognitive fatigue for frontline staff and accelerates the resolution of complex exceptions.

