{"type":"bullets","design":"S_001","title":"Continuous feedback and model optimization","lead":"Structured telemetry, weekly agent reviews, and prompt tuning keep recommendations accurate over time.","points":["Real-time telemetry logging: Capture response latency, recommendation acceptance rates, and override reasons across every gate transaction in BigQuery.","In-workflow agent ratings: Enable gate staff to flag unhelpful routing suggestions with a single click directly inside the podium interface.","Weekly champion review sessions: Conduct structured working sessions with hub gate agents to analyze edge cases during irregular operations.","Continuous prompt and grounding updates: Refine Vertex AI system instructions and refresh policy document indexes whenever airline tariff rules change.","Automated regression evaluation: Run golden dataset test suites in Vertex AI before promoting updated prompts or model versions to production gates."],"callout":{"label":"Closed-loop governance","title":"Grounded in real gate operations","text":"Every agent override and policy update feeds a weekly optimization cycle in Vertex AI, keeping rebooking recommendations aligned with live airline procedures and hub realities. Routine evaluations highlight emerging edge cases across routes, letting engineers adjust retrieval thresholds before minor inconsistencies affect customer journeys."},"notes":"Maintaining high accuracy across seasonal schedule changes requires a disciplined optimization loop. We combine automated telemetry in BigQuery with weekly frontline review sessions to refine prompts and grounding documents continuously.

