{"type":"cards","design":"S_003","title":"Pricing options","lead":"Three engagement models match delivery risk and team capacity. Pricing is confirmed after the scoping workshop.","items":[{"title":"Fixed-scope milestone delivery","text":"Structured around defined deliverables for the Vertex AI gate assistant, including data integration, policy grounding, and pilot gate rollout. This model fits best when functional requirements, passenger rebooking rules, and system interfaces are locked prior to kick-off, giving operational stakeholders predictable milestone sign-offs across each implementation phase.","icon":"clipboard"},{"title":"Dedicated agile pod capacity","text":"Provides a cross-functional team of cloud engineers, data specialists, and artificial intelligence architects working in iterative sprints alongside airline staff. This model fits best when gate agent workflows and exception handling rules require rapid testing and refinement based on live feedback from airport concourse trials.","icon":"team"},{"title":"Managed lifecycle and scale","text":"Combines initial build sprints with ongoing operational management, continuous model monitoring, and follow-the-sun engineering support after launch. This model fits best when internal technology teams want long-term operational coverage for Vertex AI performance, hallucination guardrails, and multi-hub expansion without adding permanent support headcount.","icon":"cloud-cycle"}],"notes":"We offer three commercial structures tailored to how Delta Air Lines prefers to govern delivery and ongoing operations. Whether you select milestone-based execution, dedicated agile pods, or a full lifecycle managed service, each option includes complete knowledge transfer. As noted on the slide, commercial totals and pricing are confirmed after the scoping workshop once integration boundaries are validated.

