{"type":"process","design":"S66_STEP_COLUMNS","title":"Pub/Sub schema enforcement and dead-letter routing","items":[{"title":"Ingest raw telemetry","tag":"Edge gateway","text":"Edge gateways and webhook listeners receive raw carrier telemetry and submit messages to the Pub/Sub ingestion API. Regional proxies ensure balanced transport load.","icon":"cloud-upload"},{"title":"Validate avro schema","tag":"Pub/Sub registry","text":"Pub/Sub checks every incoming message against the central Avro schema registry for required shipment ID, timestamp and coordinate types. Invalid inputs fail upfront.","icon":"shield-code"},{"title":"Route valid events","tag":"Primary topic","text":"Payloads passing strict Avro validation publish to the primary telemetry topic for immediate streaming pull by Dataflow. Workers process events in real time.","icon":"workflow-path"},{"title":"Divert malformed payloads","tag":"Dead-letter queue","text":"Payloads failing schema validation or delivery retries route to the dead-letter queue, preventing worker pipeline stalls. Teams review poison messages offline.","icon":"shield-gear"}],"notes":"Enforcing strict Avro schemas at the Pub/Sub ingestion boundary prevents corrupt GPS coordinates or missing shipment IDs from breaking downstream Dataflow jobs. Records that fail validation or exhaust delivery retries are automatically diverted to a dead-letter queue for inspection.

