{"type":"diagram","design":"S66_LAYER_STACK","title":"Dataflow Streaming Engine pipeline architecture","lead":"Dataflow Streaming Engine decouples compute from state storage to process over 1,000,000 messages per second.","layers":[{"label":"Ingestion pull layer","items":["Streaming pull subscriptions continuously ingest high-volume events with minimal delivery latency.","Avro deserialization workers parse incoming binary payloads directly into structured record formats.","Schema validation routers check payload structures immediately and isolate malformed events into sinks."],"icon":"analytics"},{"label":"Stateless compute tier","items":["The n2d-standard-4 worker pool provides reliable compute capacity to execute core transformation logic.","A horizontal CPU autoscaler adjusts VM counts based on real-time backlog growth and processing demand.","Sub-second stage processors execute stateful operations quickly to prevent downstream data bottlenecks."],"icon":"server"},{"label":"Streaming engine backend","items":["An offloaded shuffle service shifts data redistribution from worker VMs to dedicated backend nodes.","Externalized state storage maintains windowing metadata outside instances to improve fault recovery.","A 1 GiB/s throughput fabric delivers sustained bandwidth across distributed stages without congesting."],"icon":"security"},{"label":"Sink delivery tier","items":["Storage Write API clients stream prepared records directly into analytical tables with exact semantics.","BigQuery stream buffers provide instant data ingestion and commit updates for low-latency dashboards.","Pub/Sub alert publishers broadcast operational anomaly notifications directly to downstream consumers."],"icon":"automation"}],"notes":"Dataflow Streaming Engine moves pipeline state and shuffle operations off the worker VMs onto a managed Google Cloud backend. Benchmarks show this architecture sustains over 1,000,000 messages per second and 1 GiB/s throughput with sub-second stage latency.

