{"type":"cards","title":"Operational runbooks for streaming failure modes","items":[{"title":"Pub/Sub dead-letter queue message spike","fix":"Inspect malformed carrier payloads in BigQuery audit table, patch Avro schema or parser, and run Dataflow replay template. This isolates corrupt inputs and resumes ingestion without dropping messages.","status":"Amber","text":"Fix: Inspect malformed carrier payloads in BigQuery audit table, patch Avro schema or parser, and run Dataflow replay template"},{"title":"Dataflow pipeline watermark stall","fix":"Check worker CPU and streaming engine quota, verify source carrier API health, and raise max-num-workers parameter. This step relieves pipeline backpressure and prevents processing delays during surges.","status":"Amber","text":"Fix: Check worker CPU and streaming engine quota, verify source carrier API health, and raise max-num-workers parameter"},{"title":"BigQuery Storage Write API throttling","fix":"Verify connection pool stream offsets, increase Enterprise Edition max autoscale slots, and redistribute append streams. This is designed to support smooth write throughput and reduces downstream commit backlogs.","status":"Amber","text":"Fix: Verify connection pool stream offsets, increase Enterprise Edition max autoscale slots, and redistribute append streams"},{"title":"Side-input route cache refresh failure","fix":"Fall back to last known good Cloud Storage manifest snapshot and restart Cloud Composer sync task. This procedure recovers orchestration state cleanly and restores pipeline scheduling without data gaps.","status":"Grey","text":"Fix: Fall back to last known good Cloud Storage manifest snapshot and restart Cloud Composer sync task"}],"notes":"To keep the streaming pipeline within target SLAs, we provide Northwind Logistics SREs with deterministic runbooks for the four primary failure modes. Dead-letter queue spikes trigger automated schema inspection and replay jobs, while watermark stalls and write throttling have clear compute scaling steps.

