{"type":"cards","design":"S66_ISSUE_ROWS","title":"Technical risks and engineering mitigation controls","stages":["Operational risk","Pipeline vulnerability","Engineering mitigation"],"present":[{"title":"Carrier schema drift","text":"Third-party logistics providers modify JSON or Avro payload fields without advance notice, threatening to break strict deserialization workers."},{"title":"GPS cellular bursts","text":"Trucks exiting remote cellular dead zones transmit cached telemetry arrays simultaneously, arriving out of sequence across regional ingress endpoints."},{"title":"Alert fatigue","text":"Retried webhook deliveries and oscillating boundary coordinates generate duplicate exception notifications for the same delayed trailer."}],"gap":["Unvalidated payload crashes","Corrupted velocity state","Duplicate dispatcher pages"],"solution":[{"title":"DLQ isolation","text":"Pub/Sub dead-letter queues trap unparseable carrier messages after failed delivery attempts so main streaming workers continue processing cleanly."},{"title":"Watermark tuning","text":"Dataflow heuristic watermarks and allowed lateness windows sequence delayed cellular bursts by event creation time before emitting alerts."},{"title":"Stateful deduplication","text":"Apache Beam state API and BigQuery Storage Write API stream offsets enforce deterministic single-event emission per shipment threshold breach."}],"takeaway":"Isolate malformed carrier records at ingestion while handling temporal jitter and duplicate suppression in Dataflow state.","notes":"This slide maps the three primary technical risks in Northwind Logistics' streaming telemetry pipeline to concrete engineering controls. Dead-letter queues in Pub/Sub prevent poisoned tracking records from blocking worker pipelines, while Dataflow watermark tuning and BigQuery Storage Write API stream offsets maintain data accuracy.

